      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. the problem is the intensity of the spikes is hard to put into numbers right now. like, some feel like a 0.89 probability shift and others feel way more absolute, like a 0.999. i've noticed they usually happen in clusters too. if i start recording these as floating point values between 0 and 1, do you think we could use something like a Bayesian framework to update the model in real-time as i feed it these \"intuition\" data points? i want the model to basically learn my internal bio-mathematical signature.",
