      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Using floating-point values between 0 and 1 for intensity seems like a practical first step to quantify your certainty. A Bayesian framework would be excellent for real-time learning because it allows you to formally update your prior beliefs (your initial intuition) as new data points arrive. This approach naturally handles the uncertainty in your subjective inputs, allowing the model to refine its internal \"signature\" as you gather more patterned examples rather than just fitting a single fixed curve.",
