      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. im worried though that the noise from external market volatility might drown out my spikes if we just use standard data. i've been thinking that my spikes actually act as a leading indicator—like a signal that exists a few seconds before the market data even reflects the change. if that's the case, should we be looking at causal inference models or maybe something that treats my inputs as exogenous variables that actually drive the probability shifts? i wanna make sure the model treats my input as the source, not just another correlated variable.",
